-- ===========================================================================================
-- Tarak - FULL production database: schema + ALL prepared marketplace data
--
-- WHAT IS IN HERE
--   * all application tables (CREATE TABLE with indexes, foreign keys, utf8mb4 / utf8mb4_unicode_ci, InnoDB, AUTO_INCREMENT)
--   * the Laravel `migrations` table with every migration already marked as applied, so
--     `php artisan migrate --force` afterwards runs ONLY migrations added in the future
--   * the marketplace as prepared locally: service categories + catalogue, 100 provider profiles (50 barber / 50 coiffeur)
--     with services, packages, weekly schedules, documents (metadata), gallery/cover/avatar references, ~5,100 customer
--     profiles with addresses, ~5,050 reviews (the ratings behind the Tarak score), ad packages / placements / featured
--     promotions, site content, finance defaults (commission, provider welcome bonus), notification-ad defaults
--   * the local activity history: appointments, service requests, offers, chats, payments, disputes, notifications, wallet
--     ledger, lifecycle events, commission reservations, admin logs, support ticket, newsletter record
--   * 3 named demo accounts (customer@ / provider@ / admin@berberimgelsin.com) with their original password hashes
--
-- ORDER OF THIS FILE: every CREATE TABLE first, then the data - service catalogue and site settings first, users and profiles
--   next, activity history last - so an interrupted import still leaves a working catalogue.
--
-- DEMO DATA NOTICE
--   All other people in this file are SYNTHETIC (e-mail domain demo.tarak.test, fake phone numbers) and flagged
--   users.is_demo = 1; they cannot log in (their passwords are unusable random hashes). They can be removed at any time with
--   `php artisan demo:purge` or Admin > Demo Veriler. The activity history belongs to the 3 named accounts and is local TEST output
--   (notes such as "FAZ4_QA..."); the 3 named accounts use a password that is written in the repository's development seeder:
--   change or delete them (the admin one first) before the site is public.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT IN HERE
--   auth tokens and sessions, cache/queue rows, push devices, integration credentials (PayTR / SMS / SMTP / Firebase / Reverb),
--   payout accounts and exact-location payloads (encrypted with the local key), one-time start codes.
--
-- HOW TO IMPORT (cPanel -> phpMyAdmin)
--   1. Select the EMPTY database you created for Tarak in the left tree (no CREATE DATABASE / USE statement inside).
--   2. Import tab -> choose this file (tarak-full-production.sql, or the much smaller tarak-full-production.sql.gz when the
--      upload limit is small) -> format SQL -> Go.
--   Import into an empty database only: there are no DROP TABLE statements on purpose, so an accidental import into a
--   database that already holds data fails instead of silently destroying it.
--
-- MySQL 8 / MariaDB 10.x compatible. No DEFINER, no routines, no triggers, no local paths.
-- ===========================================================================================

